# IDE
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Claude Code local agent/tool settings — machine-specific (e.g. settings.local.json can carry
# local paths or permission grants) and not part of the project.
#
# `.claude/*` (contents) rather than `.claude/` (the directory itself) is deliberate: git cannot
# re-include anything inside an EXCLUDED directory, so a blanket `.claude/` would make the negation
# below impossible. `.claude/skills/` holds the Spec Kit skill definitions, which ARE project files
# — 15 of them are already tracked, and the whole spec-driven workflow depends on them being shared
# rather than local. Under a blanket ignore those 15 would stay tracked (gitignore never untracks)
# but any NEW or renamed skill would silently vanish from `git status` and never get committed —
# exactly the kind of invisible drift this repo cannot afford across two machines.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Misc
*.log

# Supabase CLI link state (project ref + local temp), never committed
supabase/.temp/

# MSYS/Git-Bash crash dumps
sh.exe.stackdump
